Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:32:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add job details endpoint and MCP tool

GET /job/:id and GET /job?url=<job link> return one job's full
description, criteria (seniority, employment type, job function,
industries), posted time, the applicant count shown on the page and
whether it still accepts applications. Removed jobs return 404 with
{ removed: true }; an invalid id or link returns 400.

The get_linkedin_job_details tool and getJobDetails() expose the same
data to MCP clients and library users. Requests run one at a time with
a fixed user agent, at least LINKEDIN_DETAIL_MIN_INTERVAL_MS apart
(default 1.5 s), and each job is cached for
LINKEDIN_DETAIL_CACHE_TTL_MS (default 6 hours).
